# Zen Finance Overview

- Source of truth: `@docs/PRD.md`.
- Product: AI-driven expense tracking via Telegram input plus a mobile-first web app.
- Primary users: 2 personal users first, with shared household support next.
- Core flow: Google SSO -> one-tap Telegram deep link -> log by voice, receipt, or text -> confirm -> review/edit on web.

# MVP Priorities

- Keep scope strict: deliver P0 before P1/P2.
- Prioritize frictionless capture, correction, and clarity over advanced automation.
- Every AI-parsed expense must be easy to confirm, edit, or replace manually.
- Link Telegram prominently on the dashboard/header; do not bury core onboarding in settings.

# Product Decisions

- Stack: Next.js 16, Tailwind CSS, Recharts, Supabase, Grammy, Groq Whisper, Gemini.
- Currency: PLN by default.
- Categories: fixed list with AI suggestion at confirmation time.
- Receipt images are not stored in v1; keep transcripted data only.
- One bot instance; map Telegram users by `telegram_id`.

# Implementation Guidance

- Prefer mobile-first UI and scale up to desktop.
- Keep the UI minimalist and calm; avoid dashboard clutter.
- Expose category summaries first; month-over-month comparisons and trend insights come later.
- Treat `Safe to Spend`, subscription prediction, and shared household features as post-MVP unless explicitly requested.
